# Running the e2e stack locally leaves its runtime state in config-test/, written by the app
# container as root: a scanned database, artwork, the activity log. Only config.toml is tracked (it is
# the fixture the stack starts from) — everything the run PRODUCES is not, or a local `docker compose
# -f docker-compose.test.yml up` leaves a dirty tree that is easy to commit by accident.
config-test/jellystructure.db
config-test/jellystructure.db-shm
config-test/jellystructure.db-wal
config-test/activity-log.json
config-test/activity-log.json.runs
config-test/livetv.json
config-test/artwork/
config-test/fingerprints/

# Python bytecode — R287 committed one by accident; running a check script must not dirty the tree.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
